[fg]
bashbasicsbyvk_loadmap.sh|||BOOTSTRAP: the loader itself. o sources it before this list is read; the loader skips it
bashbasicsbyvk_loadtime.sh|||the load-time recorder: first, so the loading of the scripts is on its timeline (o runs _lt_init right after it)
bashbasicsbyvk_smartload.sh|||the loading bar; its shims are called by print / smartmenu, so it loads before them
bashbasicsbyvk_print.sh|||the `print` command shim; reads what the last frame drew
bashbasicsbyvk_smartmenu.sh|||smart menus + the `read` shim every prompt goes through
bashbasicsbyvk_menuchrome.sh|||footer keys / menu chrome
bashbasicsbyvk_cmdmap.sh|||the command-map engine (typed words, hints); loads the menucommands files it is asked for
bashbasicsbyvk_cheatcode.sh|||cc cheat codes: _CC_PREFILL is read by the input readers
bashbasicsbyvk_viewport.sh|||draws the main list (first paint) and reads keys
bashbasicsbyvk_mouse.sh|||mouse / touch on (a terminal setup step before the first paint)
bashbasicsbyvk_engine_target.sh|||which CPU / OS binaries fit this machine
bashbasicsbyvk_engine_heal.sh|||offers a reinstall when the install was carried to another machine (checked before the first paint)
bashbasicsbyvk_displayer.sh|||builds the item rows of a folder
bashbasicsbyvk_browse.sh|||the main-loop input reader and header / footer
bashbasicsbyvk_maincommands.sh|||the MAIN commands of the command map: the hint row of the first paint reads them
bashbasicsbyvk_lock.sh|||lock marks drawn in the list
bashbasicsbyvk_fileapi_lib.sh|||FileAPI config reader used by the pending hint (split candidate: only _bb_cfg_val is needed before the first paint)
bashbasicsbyvk_staging_pending.sh|||the "unfinished uploads" hint of the main screen (split candidate: only the count / hint are needed)
bashbasicsbyvk_select.sh|||selection (.s) state: the header counts it
bashbasicsbyvk_display_filter.sh|||the .d display filter: it narrows the first list
bashbasicsbyvk_favourites.sh|||favourites mode: decides which list is drawn
bashbasicsbyvk_settings.sh|||settings file reader, timezone, defaults: every screen reads these
bashbasicsbyvk_colors.sh|||colour settings applied at start
bashbasicsbyvk_filter.sh|||the filter (=) input reader the main prompt uses
bashbasicsbyvk_notify.sh|||notification count in the header

